    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420">

                <pb facs="0766" n="672" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg672"/>

                <head>No. 420.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Manning to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 30, 1886</date>.
                        (Received December 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 25.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Under your instruction<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d420-f1"/> No. 18 of 20th instant, relative to a notice to Americans
                    published by this legation in August last, I addressed a note to Mr. Mariscal
                    setting forth the position of the United States Government with regard to the
                    doctrine of involuntary change of allegiance, as embodied in Article I, Chapter
                    V, of the Mexican Law of Foreigners, and herewith inclosed I transmit copy of my
                    note to Mr. Mariscal.</p>
                <p>In this connection I deem it proper to inclose a circular letter issued by this
                    legation to the consular officers of the United States in Mexico under date of
                    the 4th ultimo.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Th. C. Manning.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d420-a1.xml" xpointer="d420-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d420-a2.xml" xpointer="d420-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
